// Pathological witness, the SILENT half: a call written entirely at the
// CAPTURED types must be refused.
//
// READ EVERY TYPE HERE AS DELIBERATELY WRONG. This is a refutation golden.
// Each type below is the type a CAPTURING instantiation computes, not the type
// the signature owes. A reader who takes these as a model of correct gandr has
// read the file backwards.
//
// WHY A SECOND FILE AND NOT A SECOND DEFINITION. Capture makes two types that
// should differ coincide as readily as it makes two that should agree diverge.
// The loud half of the fault is a refusal; a repair verified only against the
// refused program proves capture stopped rejecting something correct and says
// nothing about what it was accepting. The two halves demand OPPOSITE
// outcomes -- the refusing witness must run clean and this one must not -- so
// they cannot share a file, and this file carries the assertion whose failure
// mode is ACCEPTANCE.
//
// THE ARITHMETIC, AND IT HAS TWO CAPTURES RATHER THAN ONE. Instantiating comp
// at (a, c, d) means a := a, b := c, c := d. Performed one parameter at a
// time, an earlier replacement is re-substituted by a later one:
//
//   comp's f expects  U[ω] (a -> F b)  --b:=c-->  a -> F c  --c:=d-->  a -> F d
//   comp's g expects  U[ω] (b -> F c)  --b:=c-->  c -> F c  --c:=d-->  d -> F d
//   comp's result     U[ω] (a -> F c)  --b:=c-->  a -> F c  --c:=d-->  a -> F d
//
// The owed types are U[ω] (a -> F c) for f and U[ω] (c -> F d) for g. BOTH
// FUNCTION EXPECTATIONS ARE CAPTURED. The result is the one component capture
// leaves correct, which is why it is the arguments and not the return type
// that carry this witness.
//
// SO A CAPTURING ENGINE ACCEPTS THIS FILE, because every type written here is
// what capture computes; and an engine that renames the binder apart REFUSES
// it, because u is then supplied at U[ω] (a -> F d) where U[ω] (a -> F c) is
// owed. The green and the red say the opposite of the usual thing: this file
// PASSING means the engine refused the program, and this file FAILING means
// the engine accepted it, which is the silent fault firing.
//
// THE ASSERTION NAMES BOTH TYPES rather than merely requiring a refusal. A
// bare refusal is satisfied by any error at all -- a name out of scope, an
// arity slip, a typo in this file -- and a refusal witness is MORE exposed to
// that than an acceptance witness, because there are far more ways to fail
// than to succeed.

//@ expect-diagnostic: type mismatch: expected U (a → F c), actual U (a → F d)

def comp(a : Type, b : Type, c : Type, f : U[ω] (a -> F b), g : U[ω] (b -> F c), x : a) -> F c {
  run y <- f(x);
  g(y)
}

// Every type in this signature is the captured one: u at the captured f
// expectation, h at the captured g expectation, and the result at the value
// capture happens to leave correct.
def captured(a : Type, b : Type, c : Type, d : Type, u : U[ω] (a -> F d), h : U[ω] (d -> F d))
  -> F (U[ω] (a -> F d))
{
  ret thunk { comp(a, c, d, u, h) }
}
